---

<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 10</p>
  <h1>Cleft sentences: <em>keep the proposition, move the spotlight</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A neutral sentence presents an event. A cleft divides the same proposition so one person, thing, time, place, reason, action, or result becomes the listener's focus. The structure can correct an assumption or organize information, but emphasis is not evidence. First recover the neutral relationship; then choose the spotlight the context supports.</p>
  <div class="meta-row"><span class="tag">70–80 min core</span><span class="tag">neutral proposition → selected focus</span><span class="tag">it, what, reason, and all patterns</span><span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span></div>
  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow"><div class="flow-step"><b>Recover</b><span>Who did what, when, where, and why?</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Select</b><span>Which supported contrast matters?</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Package</b><span>Build the cleft without duplicate roles.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Deliver</b><span>Place spoken focus and state the evidence.</span></div></div>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can recover the neutral proposition behind a cleft; use it-clefts to select a person, thing, time, place, or reason; use <span class="ex">what</span>-clefts and reversed pseudo-clefts to frame an action, need, concern, or result; use reason and <span class="ex">all</span> patterns without mechanical rules; preserve subject and object gaps, tense, agreement, and natural pronoun case; distinguish cleft focus from restrictive relative clauses and ordinary identifying clauses; hear reduced links and nuclear stress in U.S. speech; choose a neutral sentence when emphasis would sound theatrical or defensive; and support every correction with evidence.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered a defining relative, subject and object roles, contrastive stress, and a cause link before repackaging the same propositions.">
    <h3>Reactivate relative roles, neutral order, and contrast</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Cleft foundation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="who joined last month">who joined last month</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the analyst">the analyst</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the error">the error</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="LEO">LEO</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Because">Because</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="which joined last month">which joined last month</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The analyst <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="who joined last month" data-hint="Use a defining relative for a person who is the subject of joined." data-fix="The analyst who joined last month identified the error.">choose</button> identified the error.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>In <span class="ex">The analyst identified the error</span>, the subject is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the analyst" data-hint="Find the participant performing identified." data-fix="The analyst is the subject and actor.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>In the same sentence, the object is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the error" data-hint="Find the thing receiving the identification action." data-fix="The error is the object.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Correct the belief that Maya sent the invoice: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="LEO" data-hint="Stress the actual sender, not every word." data-fix="LEO sent the invoice, not Maya.">choose</button> sent the invoice.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Because" data-hint="Introduce the documented cause before the result clause." data-fix="Because the data was incomplete, we delayed the decision.">choose</button> the data was incomplete, we delayed the decision.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: the evidence stays constant while the correction changes</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Lakeside pedestrian pilot review</h3>
    <p><b>Neutral record:</b> New independent safety evidence changed the committee's position at its May 12 meeting. The evidence showed a 27% reduction in vehicle-pedestrian conflicts during a six-month trial. The committee approved a second six-month trial, not a permanent citywide policy.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">It was the new safety evidence that changed the committee's position, not political pressure.</span> The it-cleft selects the cause and corrects one proposed alternative.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">It was at the May 12 meeting that the committee changed its position.</span> The same event now spotlights time.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">What changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence.</span> The open variable comes first; the evidence fills it.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">All the committee approved was a second six-month trial.</span> The <span class="ex">all</span>-cleft limits the scope and blocks the stronger permanent-policy claim.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the shared proposition and identified cause, time, open variable, limited scope, and evidence-based contrast.">
    <h3>Discovery check: proposition, focus, and implication</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Cleft discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the new safety evidence changed the committee's position">the new safety evidence changed the committee's position</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the causal factor">the causal factor</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the May 12 meeting time">the May 12 meeting time</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an open variable followed by its value">an open variable followed by its value</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a second six-month trial and nothing stronger">a second six-month trial and nothing stronger</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the source must support the correction">the source must support the correction</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="every emphasized claim becomes true">every emphasized claim becomes true</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The neutral relationship behind the first and third clefts is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the new safety evidence changed the committee's position" data-hint="Remove the cleft frame and recover subject, verb, and object." data-fix="The new safety evidence changed the committee's position.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>In <span class="ex">It was the new safety evidence that...</span>, the focus is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the causal factor" data-hint="The focused phrase contrasts evidence with political pressure." data-fix="The it-cleft selects the causal factor.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>In <span class="ex">It was at the May 12 meeting that...</span>, the focus is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the May 12 meeting time" data-hint="The prepositional phrase after be locates when the change occurred." data-fix="The cleft spotlights the May 12 meeting time.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The <span class="ex">what</span>-cleft presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an open variable followed by its value" data-hint="What changed the position creates a slot; the evidence identifies its value." data-fix="The what-clause frames an open variable, and the complement supplies the value.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="ex">All the committee approved...</span> limits approval to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a second six-month trial and nothing stronger" data-hint="All narrows the scope and rejects a permanent-policy interpretation." data-fix="The approved scope was a second six-month trial, not permanent adoption.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Before using a cleft to correct a public account, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the source must support the correction" data-hint="Information structure can highlight a claim but cannot prove it." data-fix="The source must support the selected correction and contrast.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: separate the proposition from the focus</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Information goal</th><th>Pattern</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>select one person or thing</td><td>It + be + focus + who/that clause</td><td>It was <b>Maya</b> who found the error.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>select time, place, method, or reason</td><td>It + be + focused phrase + that clause</td><td>It was <b>on Tuesday</b> that we voted.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>frame an action, need, or concern</td><td>What + clause + be + focus</td><td>What we need is <b>a new test</b>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>put the value first</td><td>Focus + be + what + clause</td><td><b>A new test</b> is what we need.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>foreground an explanation</td><td>The reason + clause + be + that clause</td><td>The reason we paused was <b>that the data changed</b>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>limit an action, request, or result</td><td>All + clause + be + focus</td><td>All we approved was <b>a second trial</b>.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>It-clefts carry a background assumption</h3><p><span class="ex">It was Maya who called</span> normally treats <span class="ex">someone called</span> as shared or accepted and identifies Maya. If no call is established, the cleft can smuggle in an unsupported assumption. Use a neutral sentence or first establish the event.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>A cleft is not simply a longer synonym</h3><p><span class="ex">The safety evidence changed the committee's position</span> is often the clearest first report. Use <span class="ex">It was the safety evidence that...</span> when a supported alternative must be corrected. Use <span class="ex">What changed the position was...</span> when the causal question is already active or you want to delay the answer until the second part.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You matched person, object, time, place, reason, open-variable, reversed, and limited-scope focuses to complete contexts.">
    <h3>Choose ten information-focus patterns</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Cleft focus choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was Maya who found the error">It was Maya who found the error</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was the error that Maya found">It was the error that Maya found</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was on Tuesday that we voted">It was on Tuesday that we voted</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was in Room B that we met">It was in Room B that we met</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was because the data changed that we paused">It was because the data changed that we paused</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="What we need is a new test">What we need is a new test</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="A new test is what we need">A new test is what we need</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The reason we paused was that the data changed">The reason we paused was that the data changed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="All we approved was a second trial">All we approved was a second trial</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The safety evidence changed the committee's position">The safety evidence changed the committee's position</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was Tuesday who voted">It was Tuesday who voted</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Correct the belief that Leo found the error; Maya did: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It was Maya who found the error" data-hint="Place the actual person after be and use who for the remaining subject gap." data-fix="It was Maya who found the error, not Leo.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Maya found the error, not the missing invoice. Focus the object: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It was the error that Maya found" data-hint="The focused thing is the understood object of found." data-fix="It was the error that Maya found.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Correct the claim that the vote happened Monday: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It was on Tuesday that we voted" data-hint="Focus the time phrase and use the standard cleft link that." data-fix="It was on Tuesday that we voted.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Correct the claim that the meeting was in Room A: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It was in Room B that we met" data-hint="Focus the place phrase after be." data-fix="It was in Room B that we met.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Correct the belief that cost caused the pause; changed data did: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It was because the data changed that we paused" data-hint="A because-clause can be the focused causal element in an it-cleft." data-fix="It was because the data changed that we paused.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The discussion already asks what resource is needed; delay the answer: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="What we need is a new test" data-hint="Frame the open need first, then supply its value." data-fix="What we need is a new test.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Put the proposed resource first, then identify its role: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="A new test is what we need" data-hint="Use a reversed pseudo-cleft with the value before be." data-fix="A new test is what we need.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Announce that an explicit explanation follows: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The reason we paused was that the data changed" data-hint="Use the reason-clause followed by be and a that-clause." data-fix="The reason we paused was that the data changed.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>Reject the claim of permanent adoption by limiting the decision: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="All we approved was a second trial" data-hint="All plus clause reduces the approved scope to one result." data-fix="All we approved was a second trial.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>No competing account is active; give the clearest first report: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The safety evidence changed the committee's position" data-hint="A neutral sentence is clearer when no contrast needs correction." data-fix="The safety evidence changed the committee's position.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the gap, link, agreement, and tense accurately</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Subject focus versus object focus</h3><p><span class="ex">It was Maya who found the error</span> contains a subject gap after <span class="ex">who</span>: Maya found it. <span class="ex">It was the error that Maya found</span> contains an object gap: Maya found the error. Do not repeat the focused role: <span class="cross">It was the error that Maya found it.</span></p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Person links and pronoun case in real U.S. English</h3><p><span class="ex">Who</span> or <span class="ex">that</span> can link a focused person. After <span class="ex">be</span>, formal edited style may prefer <span class="ex">It was I who called</span>, but <span class="ex">It was me who called</span> is natural and widespread in conversation. Do not mark conversational object case as universally wrong. Match the register.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Agreement after a <span class="ex">what</span>-clause</h3><p>Singular <span class="ex">is</span> is common when the <span class="ex">what</span>-clause is treated as one need or issue: <span class="ex">What we need is two more chairs.</span> Plural agreement also occurs when speakers align with a plural complement: <span class="ex">What we need are two more chairs.</span> Avoid tests that pretend only one is possible. Use an unambiguously singular focus when agreement itself is being assessed.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Reason and <span class="ex">all + do</span> variation</h3><p><span class="ex">The reason we paused was that the data changed</span> is a concise careful target. <span class="ex">The reason is because...</span> is widespread in conversation and published English; it can sound redundant to some readers, so revise it when concision matters rather than calling it impossible. After <span class="ex">all + do</span>, both <span class="ex">All I did was call</span> and <span class="ex">All I did was to call</span> occur; bare <span class="ex">call</span> is common in U.S. English.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You preserved subject and object gaps, natural person links, register-sensitive pronouns, tense, singular focus, and defensible reason and all patterns.">
    <h3>Complete eleven form and variation decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Cleft form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="who found the error">who found the error</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="that Maya found">that Maya found</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="who called">who called</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="that we voted">that we voted</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="What changed the position was the new evidence">What changed the position was the new evidence</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="What we need is a clear deadline">What we need is a clear deadline</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="A clear deadline is what we need">A clear deadline is what we need</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The reason we paused was that the sample changed">The reason we paused was that the sample changed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="All I did was call the office">All I did was call the office</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It had been Maya who had found the error">It had been Maya who had found the error</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It is tomorrow that the review begins">It is tomorrow that the review begins</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="that Maya found it">that Maya found it</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Maya is the focused actor: It was Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="who found the error" data-hint="Use who followed directly by the verb because Maya fills the subject gap." data-fix="It was Maya who found the error.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The error is the focused object: It was the error <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="that Maya found" data-hint="Keep Maya as the subject and leave the object gap after found." data-fix="It was the error that Maya found.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>In natural conversation, identify yourself as the caller: It was me <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="who called" data-hint="Conversational me after be is natural; who links the person to the subject gap." data-fix="It was me who called.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Correct the claim that the completed vote happened Monday: It was Tuesday <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="that we voted" data-hint="Keep the completed vote in the past and link the focused time to the remaining clause." data-fix="It was Tuesday that we voted.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The complete accurate future-time cleft is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It is tomorrow that the review begins" data-hint="Use present be in the cleft frame and Present Simple for the scheduled event." data-fix="It is tomorrow that the review begins.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Match the B2 assessment's singular focused cause: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="What changed the position was the new evidence" data-hint="The what-clause acts as subject; do not add it." data-fix="What changed the position was the new evidence.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Use an unambiguously singular complement: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="What we need is a clear deadline" data-hint="One clear deadline supports singular is without an agreement dispute." data-fix="What we need is a clear deadline.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Reverse that pseudo-cleft: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="A clear deadline is what we need" data-hint="Place the focused value first and the what-clause second." data-fix="A clear deadline is what we need.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>Use the concise careful reason pattern: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The reason we paused was that the sample changed" data-hint="Introduce the reason content with that." data-fix="The reason we paused was that the sample changed.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>Use a natural U.S. bare infinitive after <span class="ex">all + did</span>: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="All I did was call the office" data-hint="Bare call is common after all I did was; do not insert an -ing form." data-fix="All I did was call the office.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">11</span><span>From a later past viewpoint, identify the earlier finder: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It had been Maya who had found the error" data-hint="The cleft frame and finding both precede the later past reference." data-fix="It had been Maya who had found the error.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep clefts separate from similar-looking clauses</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Structure</th><th>Job</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>it-cleft</td><td>select a focus inside a proposition</td><td>It was Maya who found it.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>referential it + relative clause</td><td>identify a previously mentioned thing</td><td>It was the report that had a blue cover.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>defining relative</td><td>identify which noun is meant</td><td>The report that Maya sent was complete.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>what-cleft</td><td>frame an open action or need, then fill it</td><td>What Maya sent was the final report.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>embedded question</td><td>report an unknown answer</td><td>I don't know what Maya sent.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>neutral declarative</td><td>report without a selected correction</td><td>Maya sent the final report.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3><span class="ex">What</span> already means “the thing that”</h3><p>In a pseudo-cleft, <span class="ex">what Maya sent</span> is a fused relative meaning “the thing that Maya sent.” Do not add a head noun directly: <span class="cross">what report Maya sent</span>. Use <span class="ex">the report that Maya sent</span> when the noun <span class="ex">report</span> must be explicit.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Standard cleft link and real variation</h3><p><span class="ex">That</span> is a reliable careful link after a focused time or place: <span class="ex">It was Tuesday that we met.</span> <span class="ex">When</span> and <span class="ex">where</span> variants occur, and some similar sentences are ordinary identifying clauses rather than canonical clefts. Teach and use <span class="ex">that</span> as the portable target without declaring every variant impossible.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished selected focus, noun identification, fused relatives, embedded questions, neutral reporting, and standard cleft links.">
    <h3>Choose ten clause functions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Cleft boundary choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was Maya who found it">It was Maya who found it</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was the report that had a blue cover">It was the report that had a blue cover</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The report that Maya sent was complete">The report that Maya sent was complete</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="What Maya sent was the final report">What Maya sent was the final report</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="I don't know what Maya sent">I don't know what Maya sent</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Maya sent the final report">Maya sent the final report</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the report that Maya sent">the report that Maya sent</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was Tuesday that we met">It was Tuesday that we met</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It was me who called">It was me who called</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The reason was that the sample changed">The reason was that the sample changed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="what report Maya sent">what report Maya sent</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Correct Leo as the assumed finder; Maya actually found it: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It was Maya who found it" data-hint="Use an it-cleft to select the actual person." data-fix="It was Maya who found it.">choose</button>.</span></div>
