  <h2>Sound natural: one nucleus carries the correction</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In U.S. speech, the cleft frame often reduces while the selected contrast receives nuclear stress. The stressed word is not permanently fixed; it depends on the correction.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Spoken line</th><th>Connection</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>It was <b>MAYA</b> who called.</td><td><span class="ex">it was</span> may reduce toward /ɪtwəz/</td><td>correct the person</td></tr>
    <tr><td>It was on <b>TUESDAY</b> that we voted.</td><td><span class="ex">that</span> may be weak /ðət/</td><td>correct the time</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What we <b>NEED</b> is a clear date.</td><td><span class="ex">what we</span> links closely /ˈwʌtwi/</td><td>frame the need; stress may fall within the first part</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What we need is a <b>CLEAR DATE</b>.</td><td>a thought-group boundary may precede <span class="ex">is</span></td><td>deliver the new value</td></tr>
    <tr><td>All we approved was a <b>SECOND TRIAL</b>.</td><td>function words reduce around the final focus</td><td>limit the approved scope</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <p>Do not stress every content word. Compare <span class="ex">It was MAYA who sent the Tuesday report</span> with <span class="ex">It was the TUESDAY report that Maya sent</span>. The proposition overlaps, but the supported correction changes the nucleus.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read reduced it-was, weak that, linked what-we, thought-group focus, and limited-scope nuclear-stress listening check" data-success-message="Correct. You recovered person, time, framed need, new value, and limited scope from five connected U.S. English clefts.">
    <h3>Listen for the selected correction</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Cleft listening choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the person Maya">the person Maya</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the time Tuesday">the time Tuesday</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the need itself">the need itself</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the new value a clear date">the new value a clear date</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the limited result a second trial">the limited result a second trial</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="every word equally">every word equally</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“It was MAYA who called.”</span> The nucleus corrects <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the person Maya" data-hint="The strongest stress falls on the actual caller." data-fix="The selected focus is the person Maya.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“It was on TUESDAY that we voted.”</span> Weak <span class="ex">that</span> leaves focus on <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the time Tuesday" data-hint="The time phrase carries the correction." data-fix="The selected focus is Tuesday.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“What we NEED is a clear date.”</span> The first-part stress foregrounds <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the need itself" data-hint="The speaker contrasts needing with another action such as preferring." data-fix="The first-part nucleus highlights the need itself.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“What we need is a CLEAR DATE.”</span> The later nucleus delivers <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the new value a clear date" data-hint="The what-clause frames the open need; the complement supplies new information." data-fix="The new focused value is a clear date.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Tutor reads: <span class="ex">“All we approved was a SECOND TRIAL.”</span> The final stress limits the decision to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the limited result a second trial" data-hint="All plus the nuclear complement excludes stronger approval." data-fix="The approved scope is limited to a second trial.">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    <details><summary>Tutor script and transcript</summary><ol><li>It was MAYA who called.</li><li>It was on TUESDAY that we voted.</li><li>What we NEED is a clear date.</li><li>What we need is a CLEAR DATE.</li><li>All we approved was a SECOND TRIAL.</li></ol><p>Read each line once naturally and once after stating the mistaken assumption. Keep the cleft frame light and the supported correction prominent.</p></details>
  </div>

  <h2>Read emphasis against the actual record</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card"><h3>Fictional Lakeside pilot file</h3>
    <p>The Lakeside committee rejected permanent adoption of a pedestrian-safety design on March 4 because the first report contained only two months of observation. A six-month independent study ended April 30. It compared the same three intersections before and during the pilot and recorded a 27% reduction in vehicle-pedestrian conflicts. The study did not measure citywide traffic.</p>
    <p>At the May 12 meeting, the committee reviewed the independent study, a 430-signature resident petition, and a budget memo. The signed decision record states that the new safety evidence changed the committee's position. It does not identify political pressure as the cause. The committee approved a second six-month trial at the same three intersections by a 6-2 vote. It did not approve permanent or citywide adoption.</p>
    <p>The accurate corrections are: <span class="ex">It was the new safety evidence that changed the committee's position</span>; <span class="ex">It was at the May 12 meeting that the position changed</span>; and <span class="ex">All the committee approved was a second six-month trial at the same three intersections.</span> The clefts make the contrasts prominent, but the study and signed record provide the evidence.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You reconstructed Lakeside's dates, sample scope, measured result, decision evidence, vote, approved scope, and explicit limits."><h3>Eight evidence-bound reading decisions</h3><div class="quiz-list">
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The committee rejected permanent adoption on March 4." data-hint="Separate the earlier decision from the May 12 change." data-fix="The committee rejected permanent adoption on March 4."><p class="quiz-question">1. What happened on March 4?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The committee rejected permanent adoption on March 4.">The committee rejected permanent adoption on March 4.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The committee approved citywide adoption on March 4.">The committee approved citywide adoption on March 4.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The independent study began after May 12.">The independent study began after May 12.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The first report contained only two months of observation." data-hint="Use the stated reason for the March decision." data-fix="The first report contained only two months of observation."><p class="quiz-question">2. Why did the committee reject permanent adoption then?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The first report contained only two months of observation.">The first report contained only two months of observation.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The first report proved a citywide result over six years.">The first report proved a citywide result over six years.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The budget memo prohibited all future research.">The budget memo prohibited all future research.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A 27% reduction in conflicts at the same three intersections." data-hint="Keep the measured result and sample scope together." data-fix="The study recorded a 27% reduction at the same three intersections."><p class="quiz-question">3. What did the six-month study measure?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A 27% reduction in conflicts at the same three intersections.">A 27% reduction in conflicts at the same three intersections.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A 27% reduction across the entire city.">A 27% reduction across the entire city.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A 430% reduction caused by a petition.">A 430% reduction caused by a petition.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The signed decision record identifies the new safety evidence." data-hint="Choose the source that directly states what changed the position." data-fix="The signed decision record identifies the new safety evidence as the factor that changed the position."><p class="quiz-question">4. What supports the focused causal correction?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The signed decision record identifies the new safety evidence.">The signed decision record identifies the new safety evidence.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The cleft grammar itself proves the cause.">The cleft grammar itself proves the cause.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="An unnamed rumor identifies political pressure.">An unnamed rumor identifies political pressure.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The position changed at the May 12 meeting." data-hint="The time-cleft selects the later meeting date." data-fix="The committee changed its position at the May 12 meeting."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which time is accurately focused?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The position changed at the May 12 meeting.">The position changed at the May 12 meeting.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The position changed permanently on March 4.">The position changed permanently on March 4.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The position changed after a future citywide study.">The position changed after a future citywide study.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The committee approved a second six-month trial by a 6-2 vote." data-hint="Keep the duration and vote count with the approved action." data-fix="The committee approved a second six-month trial by a 6-2 vote."><p class="quiz-question">6. What was the documented decision?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The committee approved a second six-month trial by a 6-2 vote.">The committee approved a second six-month trial by a 6-2 vote.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The committee approved permanent citywide adoption unanimously.">The committee approved permanent citywide adoption unanimously.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The committee rejected every additional trial by 2-6.">The committee rejected every additional trial by 2-6.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The approved scope remained the same three intersections, not the entire city." data-hint="Use the explicit geographic limit." data-fix="The second trial remained at the same three intersections."><p class="quiz-question">7. What does the <span class="ex">all</span>-cleft need to preserve?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The approved scope remained the same three intersections, not the entire city.">The approved scope remained the same three intersections, not the entire city.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All means the committee approved every possible location.">All means the committee approved every possible location.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The study measured no intersections at all.">The study measured no intersections at all.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The cleft highlights the supported correction; the study and signed record supply the evidence." data-hint="Separate information focus from proof." data-fix="The cleft highlights; the underlying sources support the claim."><p class="quiz-question">8. Which final statement treats emphasis responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The cleft highlights the supported correction; the study and signed record supply the evidence.">The cleft highlights the supported correction; the study and signed record supply the evidence.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Any claim placed in a cleft becomes factual without a source.">Any claim placed in a cleft becomes factual without a source.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because clefts emphasize, neutral evidence is unnecessary.">Because clefts emphasize, neutral evidence is unnecessary.</button></div></div>
  </div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>Build the supported spotlight from shuffled chunks</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="it was the new safety evidence that changed the committee's position" data-hint="Start with the it-cleft frame, place the supported causal focus after was, and finish the that-clause." data-fix="It was the new safety evidence that changed the committee's position." data-success-message="Correct. The it-cleft selects the documented cause and preserves the neutral proposition."><h3>Builder 1: causal correction</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the correction to the political-pressure claim.</p><div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="changed">changed</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="it was">It was</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="position">position</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the new">the new</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="that">that</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="committee's">committee's</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="safety evidence">safety evidence</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button></div><div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="what changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence" data-hint="Build the what-clause as subject, then was and the singular focused value." data-fix="What changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence." data-success-message="Correct. The pseudo-cleft frames the causal variable before supplying the documented evidence."><h3>Builder 2: open variable and value</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the B2 assessment pattern.</p><div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the committee's">the committee's</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the new">the new</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="what">What</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="was">was</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="position">position</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="safety evidence">safety evidence</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="changed">changed</button></div><div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="all the committee approved was a second six-month trial" data-hint="Open with all plus the clause, then was and the limited approved result." data-fix="All the committee approved was a second six-month trial." data-success-message="Correct. The all-cleft limits the decision to the documented second trial."><h3>Builder 3: scope limit</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the correction to permanent adoption.</p><div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a second">a second</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="approved">approved</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="trial">trial</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="all">All</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="six-month">six-month</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the committee">the committee</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="was">was</button></div><div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the broken information structure</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="it" data-hint="The what-clause already functions as the subject." data-fix="What changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence." data-why="Adding it duplicates the subject role between the what-clause and the linking verb." data-success-message="Correct. The what-clause now connects directly to was and its focused value."><h3>Repair 1: duplicate subject</h3><p>Tap the unnecessary pronoun.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="what">What changed the committee's position</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it">it</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="was">was</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="evidence">the new safety evidence.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="it" data-hint="The focused error already fills the object gap after found." data-fix="It was the error that Maya found." data-why="Repeating it after found creates two objects for one role." data-success-message="Correct. The that-clause now contains an object gap filled by the focused error."><h3>Repair 2: duplicate object</h3><p>Tap the repeated object.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="frame">It was</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="error">the error</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="clause">that Maya found</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it">it.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="which" data-hint="A focused person takes who or that in the portable target." data-fix="It was Elena who identified the mismatch." data-why="Which normally links a thing, while who or that connects the focused person to the subject gap." data-success-message="Correct. The person focus now has an appropriate link."><h3>Repair 3: person link</h3><p>Tap the relative word that mismatches the focused person.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="frame">It was</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="elena">Elena</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="which">which</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="identified">identified the mismatch.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="cleft" data-hint="The record does not establish that political pressure changed the position." data-fix="The signed record says it was the new safety evidence that changed the committee's position." data-why="A grammatical cleft can foreground a claim, but it cannot replace source evidence or reverse the documented cause." data-success-message="Correct. The focused correction now follows the signed record instead of unsupported rhetoric."><h3>Repair 4: emphasis is not evidence</h3><p>Tap the unsupported focus claim.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="despite">Despite the signed record,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="cleft">it was political pressure that changed the position</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="proof">because the cleft sounds convincing.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>Say the supported correction before you reveal it</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform><p class="note-line">Respond aloud first. State the neutral proposition, name the mistaken assumption, build the cleft, and place one nuclear stress. Then reveal and compare.</p><div class="transform-list">
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> The record identifies safety evidence, not political pressure, as the cause.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It was the new SAFETY EVIDENCE that changed the committee's position.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> The change happened at the May 12 meeting, not on March 4.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It was at the MAY 12 MEETING that the committee changed its position.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> Frame the open causal question, then identify the evidence.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>What changed the committee's position was the new SAFETY EVIDENCE.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Limit the approved action to a second six-month trial.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>All the committee approved was a SECOND SIX-MONTH TRIAL.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> No mistaken assumption is active; report the cause plainly.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The new safety evidence changed the committee's position.</strong></p></div>
  </div></div>

  <h2>Practice correction without exposing private disputes</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to discuss a real accusation, workplace dispute, political belief, legal case, medical decision, relationship conflict, academic complaint, financial decision, immigration matter, or identifying public controversy. Use Lakeside or a tutor-created record. The skill is accurate information focus, not winning an argument through dramatic grammar.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Proposition map:</b> Use Lakeside or another fictional record. Write three neutral subject-verb-object propositions and list one supported competing assumption for each before choosing any cleft.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Spotlight switch:</b> Keep one proposition constant and focus the actor, object, time, place, and reason in five versions. State what each version presupposes and corrects.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Pseudo-cleft switch:</b> Frame an open need or cause with a what-clause, then reverse the pseudo-cleft so the focused value comes first. Explain the discourse difference.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register switch:</b> Identify yourself once with formal subject case and once with natural conversational object case. Then revise a widespread reason-because pattern for concise edited prose.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Evidence close:</b> Give the neutral record, source, selected correction, excluded alternative, and scope limit. Remove the cleft if no real contrast needs attention.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card"><h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second evidence-based correction</h3><p>Use Lakeside or a new fictional file. Begin with three neutral propositions and the source for each. Correct one person or thing, one time or place, and one cause using three it-clefts. Use one what-cleft, one reversed pseudo-cleft, one reason pattern, and one <span class="ex">all</span>-cleft. Include a subject gap, an object gap, a natural pronoun choice for the register, and one tense other than Past Simple.</p><p>State the background assumption each cleft invites, the competing claim it corrects, and the evidence supporting the focus. Deliver three different nuclear stresses. Then replace one cleft with a neutral sentence because no contrast is active. Your partner changes the evidence or asks what remains presupposed; revise immediately.</p><p><b>Listener check:</b> Can the listener recover the neutral proposition, focused constituent, missing clause role, presupposed background, excluded alternative, register, evidence source, and scope limit?</p></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved neutral relationships, focus, gaps, variation, spoken prominence, and evidence limits."><h3>Seven final decisions</h3><div class="quiz-list">
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="What changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence." data-hint="The B2 assessment uses a what-clause as subject and a singular focused cause after was." data-fix="What changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence matches the B2 exit-assessment focus?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="What changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence.">What changed the committee's position was the new safety evidence.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="What it changed the committee was the evidence position.">What it changed the committee was the evidence position.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It what changed was the committee evidence.">It what changed was the committee evidence.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It was the safety evidence that changed the position, not political pressure." data-hint="The signed record supports evidence as the cause and explicitly does not support political pressure." data-fix="It was the safety evidence that changed the position."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which it-cleft makes the supported causal correction?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It was the safety evidence that changed the position, not political pressure.">It was the safety evidence that changed the position, not political pressure.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It was political pressure that changed the position because emphasis proves it.">It was political pressure that changed the position because emphasis proves it.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It what safety evidence was position changed.">It what safety evidence was position changed.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It was the error that Maya found." data-hint="The focused error fills the object gap; do not repeat it." data-fix="It was the error that Maya found."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which object-focus cleft contains one complete object role?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It was the error that Maya found.">It was the error that Maya found.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It was the error that Maya found it.">It was the error that Maya found it.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It the error was that found Maya.">It the error was that found Maya.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It was me who called." data-hint="Natural conversational U.S. English commonly uses object case after be." data-fix="It was me who called."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence is natural conversational self-identification?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It was me who called.">It was me who called.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It was me which called.">It was me which called.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It me was who call.">It me was who call.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The reason we paused was that the sample changed." data-hint="Use the concise careful target without claiming conversational because is impossible." data-fix="The reason we paused was that the sample changed."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which version is concise for an edited report?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The reason we paused was that the sample changed.">The reason we paused was that the sample changed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The reason what paused it because sample.">The reason what paused it because sample.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because reason was the sample which pause.">Because reason was the sample which pause.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="All the committee approved was a second six-month trial at three intersections." data-hint="The all-cleft must retain duration and geographic scope." data-fix="All the committee approved was a second six-month trial at three intersections."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which line blocks an unsupported permanent citywide interpretation?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All the committee approved was a second six-month trial at three intersections.">All the committee approved was a second six-month trial at three intersections.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All means the committee permanently approved every street.">All means the committee permanently approved every street.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="What all city approved because permanent.">What all city approved because permanent.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A cleft selects the supported focus; the underlying study and signed record support the claim." data-hint="Separate information packaging from proof." data-fix="The cleft selects focus, while evidence supports the content."><p class="quiz-question">7. Which conclusion treats emphasis responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A cleft selects the supported focus; the underlying study and signed record support the claim.">A cleft selects the supported focus; the underlying study and signed record support the claim.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A cleft makes any unsupported accusation true.">A cleft makes any unsupported accusation true.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If a sentence is neutral, it can never report evidence clearly.">If a sentence is neutral, it can never report evidence clearly.</button></div></div>
  </div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>Reflect: does the spotlight serve the listener?</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card"><h3>Explain the information design</h3><p>Complete these lines aloud: <span class="ex">The neutral proposition is...</span> <span class="ex">The supported focus is...</span> <span class="ex">The background assumption is...</span> <span class="ex">The competing claim is...</span> <span class="ex">The gap is subject / object / adjunct...</span> <span class="ex">This pattern fits because...</span> <span class="ex">The nucleus falls on...</span> <span class="ex">The source establishes...</span> <span class="ex">A neutral sentence would be better if...</span></p><p>Then move the nucleus, reverse a pseudo-cleft, or remove the evidence for the contrast. Reformulate and explain how the information structure or responsible claim must change.</p><p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Next use:</b> Before the next lesson, retrieve one person-focus it-cleft, one object-focus it-cleft, one what-cleft, one all-cleft, and one neutral alternative from five new fictional records. State the proposition and evidence first.</div>
